P0118 The existing tests pass, but additional local checks expose failures on ordinary empty results, optional metadata and callback reuse. I found 8 High, 2 Medium and findings. No repository source was changed; regression tests and compile-only examples are in [review-harness](/work/tmp/review-harness).


P0119 High


P0120 Empty native results produce invalid Rust slices


P0121 Locations: [buf.rs:47](/work/crate/src/buf.rs:47), [remote.rs:387](/work/crate/src/remote.rs:387), [diff.rs:1281](/work/crate/src/diff.rs:1281).


P0122 Expected: empty buffers, reference advertisements and binary payloads are readable as empty slices.


P0123 Observed: these wrappers pass null pointers with length zero to `slice::from_raw_parts`, which requires a non-null pointer even for empty slices. Separate regression tests for `Buf::new().is_empty()`, listing references from a newly initialized local repository, and reading a binary-only diff payload each terminated with SIGABRT on Rust 1.99.1.


P0124 Consequence: ordinary inspection can terminate the application. Normalize empty results before constructing slices; also fix `Buf::deref_mut` at line 53. Add empty-result regression tests.


P0125 Nullable metadata getters panic on valid objects


P0126 Locations: [merge.rs:56](/work/crate/src/merge.rs:56), [rebase.rs:319](/work/crate/src/rebase.rs:319), [refspec.rs:37](/work/crate/src/refspec.rs:37).


P0127 Executed tests reproduced three cases:


P0128 Revision ranges include the excluded left endpoint. src/revwalk.rs:132. Revwalk::push_range does not establish the exclusion side of a two-dot revision range. On a linear history A <- B <- C, pushing B..C also yields B and A instead of yielding only C, because the left endpoint is traversed as another root. Consumers using two-dot ranges to select newly introduced commits consequently process commits outside the requested range.


P0129 - `find_annotated_commit(id)?.refname()` panics because lookup by ID supplies no reference name.
- `exec()` on an ordinary rebase `Pick` panics, despite documentation saying this field is populated only for `Exec`.
- `dst()` for the accepted fetch refspec `refs/heads/main` panics because its destination is absent.


P0130 Expected: the optional string accessors return `None`. Observed: their implementations unwrap nullable native fields.


P0131 Consequence: callers cannot safely inspect otherwise valid objects. Propagate absence through the string accessors and provide optional byte accessors where the existing slice return type cannot represent absence. Existing smoke tests omit these cases.


P0132 Moving configured callback options leaves stale payload pointers


P0133 Locations: [apply.rs:127](/work/crate/src/apply.rs:127), [apply.rs:140](/work/crate/src/apply.rs:140), [stash.rs:132](/work/crate/src/stash.rs:132).


P0134 Expected: configured Rust options remain usable after ordinary moves, including returning them from a helper or placing them in a `Box`.


P0135 Observed: callback setters store the current address of `self`; `raw()` does not refresh it. Two executed tests configured callbacks, moved the options into boxes, and confirmed that their exported payloads still contained the previous stack addresses.


P0136 Consequence: subsequent native callbacks access the old location. This was established by pointer comparison and source inspection; callbacks were not invoked through stale pointers.


P0137 Refresh payloads immediately before native calls, or store callback state at a stable owned address. Add move-after-configuration tests.


P0138 `into_inner` leaves the old revision filter installed


P0139 [revwalk.rs:43](/work/crate/src/revwalk.rs:43).


P0140 Expected: consuming `RevwalkWithHideCb` releases its callback and returns an independently usable walker.


P0141 Observed: `into_inner()` only resets the native walker. Native reset preserves its callback and payload. An executed three-commit regression subsequently pushed the tip and hid the base: the supposedly detached callback ran four times and incorrectly removed the tip.


P0142 Consequence: results remain filtered unexpectedly. Moreover, the returned type releases the Rust callback borrow while native code retains its pointer.


P0143 Explicitly unregister the callback before returning the walker. The existing test misses this because its subsequent walk does not reactivate limited traversal.


P0144 A refspec can outlive its owning remote


P0145 [remote.rs:283](/work/crate/src/remote.rs:283).


P0146 Expected: a borrowed `Refspec` cannot outlive its `Remote`.


P0147 Observed: `get_refspec` returns `Refspec<'repo>`, tying it to the repository instead. A compile-only example successfully returns a refspec obtained from a local remote that is dropped before the function returns. Supporting native source confirms that `git_remote_free` frees these refspecs.


P0148 Consequence: ordinary helper functions can return dangling handles through safe Rust.


P0149 Tie the return lifetime to the receiver borrow. Evidence is successful compilation plus ownership inspection; expired data was not accessed.


P0150 Pathspec diff matches can outlive their diff


P0151 [pathspec.rs:63](/work/crate/src/pathspec.rs:63).


P0152 Expected: matching diff entries remain valid for the lifetime of the returned match list.


P0153 Observed: `match_diff` ties its result only to `self`. A compile-only example successfully returns matches from a locally created diff. Native implementation inspection shows the match list stores pointers to the original diff deltas without retaining or copying their owner.


P0154 Consequence: callers can retain a match list after its entries have been freed.


P0155 Borrow both the pathspec and diff for the result’s lifetime, or retain owned native data. Add a compile-fail lifetime regression.


P0156 Rebases can outlive their callback options


P0157 Locations: [repo.rs:2289](/work/crate/src/repo.rs:2289), [repo.rs:2313](/work/crate/src/repo.rs:2313).


P0158 Expected: callbacks and checkout configuration used by later `next()` or `abort()` calls remain alive.


P0159 Observed: returned rebases borrow only the repository. A compile-only example successfully returns a rebase configured with local options and a callback capturing a local variable. Native `rebase_alloc` shallow-copies the checkout options, including their pointers; it does not retain the Rust owners.


P0160 Consequence: subsequent rebase operations can access dropped callback or configuration state.


P0161 Make the rebase retain ownership or a borrow of the required options. Evidence is compilation and source inspection; the expired callback was not executed.


P0162 Message prettification panics on legacy-encoded bytes


P0163 [message.rs:32](/work/crate/src/message.rs:32).


P0164 Expected: the `IntoCString` API either produces a valid `String` or returns an error for non-UTF-8 output.


P0165 Observed: `message_prettify(&b"caf\xe9\n"[..], None)` panicked at `as_str().unwrap()` in an executed regression.


P0166 Consequence: processing a legitimate legacy-encoded Git message unwinds instead of returning the advertised `Result`.


P0167 Convert UTF-8 validation failure into an error and test both UTF-8 and legacy-encoded messages.


P0168 Medium


P0169 `skip_reuc` changes conflict handling instead


P0170 [merge.rs:98](/work/crate/src/merge.rs:98).


P0171 Expected: `skip_reuc` controls writing the REUC extension independently of conflict handling.


P0172 Observed: it changes `GIT_MERGE_FAIL_ON_CONFLICT`. Executed conflicting-merge tests showed that `skip_reuc(true)` returns error −24 instead of a conflicted index, while `fail_on_conflict(true).skip_reuc(false)` unexpectedly permits that index.


P0173 Consequence: callers receive different merge outcomes merely by configuring extension output.


P0174 Use `GIT_MERGE_SKIP_REUC` and test both settings independently and together.


P0175 `Time` ordering disagrees with equality


P0176 [time.rs:57](/work/crate/src/time.rs:57).


P0177 Expected: `cmp` returns `Equal` exactly when `Eq` does.


P0178 Observed: derived equality includes the timezone sign, while ordering compares only seconds and offset. An executed test read a commit signature containing `-0000` and compared it with the equivalent `Time::new(..., 0)`: ordering reported equality, but `Eq` reported inequality.


P0179 Consequence: ordered collections treat distinct values as the same key.


P0180 Make equality and ordering use the same fields, including the sign if its distinction is retained. Add negative-zero timestamp coverage.


P0181 Low


P0182 Public failure contracts are incomplete


P0183 Representative locations: [build.rs:177](/work/crate/src/build.rs:177), [pathspec.rs:172](/work/crate/src/pathspec.rs:172).


P0184 The advisory pass reported 428 missing `# Errors`, 117 missing `# Panics` and 17 missing `# Safety` sections in `src/`. Some constraints already appear in prose, and some panic diagnostics concern invariants; these are diagnostic counts, not additional bug counts.


P0185 Confirmed omissions include NUL-triggered builder panics and path restrictions enforced through `unwrap`. Document actual caller obligations and recoverable failures.


P0186 Public handles frequently lack `Debug`


P0187 Representative locations: [index.rs:17](/work/crate/src/index.rs:17), [repo.rs:109](/work/crate/src/repo.rs:109).


P0188 The advisory pass identified 113 public types without `Debug`. This prevents standard diagnostic patterns such as calling `unwrap_err()` on a result whose successful value is `Index`.


P0189 Provide useful manual implementations where deriving would expose inappropriate internals or require formatting callbacks.


P0190 Native invariants lack consistent justification


P0191 Representative locations: [oid_array.rs:24](/work/crate/src/oid_array.rs:24), [rebase.rs:88](/work/crate/src/rebase.rs:88).


P0192 The advisory pass emitted 799 undocumented-block diagnostics across 798 distinct reported locations, plus eight unsafe-implementation diagnostics. Some sites contain equivalent prose.


P0193 The concrete maintenance concern is that nullability and owner-lifetime assumptions are difficult to verify—the same assumptions implicated above. Document validated native contracts at these boundaries; missing comments alone are not evidence of further undefined behavior.


P0194 Broad lint allowances weaken the documentation gate


P0195 Locations: [lib.rs:69](/work/crate/src/lib.rs:69), [lib.rs:150](/work/crate/src/lib.rs:150).


P0196 There were 109 allowance-without-reason diagnostics across 16 distinct locations, including macro expansions. Generated public convenience methods explicitly bypass `deny(missing_docs)`, so a passing documentation check does not establish complete public documentation.


P0197 Staging a buffer retains the input entry object ID and size. src/index.rs:225. Index::add_frombuffer copies entry.id and entry.file_size into the native index entry without replacing them from the supplied data. Reusing an entry with an older blob ID and file_size = 1 to stage a 20-byte replacement therefore leaves the stored index pointing to the older blob with the stale size. Writing a tree from that index records the old content instead of the replacement buffer.


P0198 Document generated methods and keep narrowly justified allowances or expectations.


P0199 Verification


P0200 All commands used installed tools and prefetched dependencies, with `RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0`, `CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true` and two build jobs. Host: aarch64 Linux, Rust/Cargo 1.99.1.


